index 0000000..ecf782b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog/5413.bugfix.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+``str()`` on the ``ExceptionInfo`` object returned by ``pytest.raises`` (and
+``pytest.raises``-like helpers) now returns the string representation of the
+wrapped exception (i.e. ``str(excinfo.value)``) instead of the traceback
+location, so it behaves like ``str()`` on a normally caught exception.
